455	101,496,576,1009	455. Flowers of Phlox.	A sprig of Phlox with two salver-shaped flowers, each a long slender tube opening into five broad, rounded lobes, one seen from the side and one from the front, above narrow calyx-teeth and leaves.
456	551,452,935,713	456. Flowers of Polemonium.	Two Polemonium flowers: one seen from the side as a cupped, nodding bell, the other face-on, almost wheel-shaped, with its stamens and three-cleft style in the centre.
457	692,790,848,1018	457. Pod of Polemonium, cut across.	The Polemonium pod cut across on its stalk, showing three cells, each holding a few seeds.
